{"title":"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of ordered pairs of positive integer solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/b/98b7e4c455672c30d743cce7506408a40cb68129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m, n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" /> to the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e58cb02756b790263193bf99d3cb9d316914ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20m + 12n = 2012$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"145\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/5/da561bf87639f148a39d4331d2633126edcb6072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = \\frac{503-3n}{5},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"117\" height=\"37\" /> so in order for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> to be an integer, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acafb86569ba1b4d112c16440bdc75fdb338ed85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n \\equiv 503 \\mod 5 \\longrightarrow n \\equiv 1 \\mod 5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"286\" height=\"14\" /> The smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is obviously <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> and the greatest is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/c/5ccf90f74d1509c92d9d3cc84687447db9ef196a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{503 - 5}{3} = 166,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"118\" height=\"37\" /> so the total number of solutions is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f62bc9e413706968d11625096a6bf59f53fdee46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{166-1}{5}+1 = \\boxed{034}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"157\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>~changed 34 to 034 (AIME solutions are always exactly 3 digits) poofypanda\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/0/7f0390009cd837c9d21e684a52fe6cee540b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5m + 3n = 503$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"118\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Thus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/831391aa0f137c20e4f21f65ce7265b441d036ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n = 503 -5m \\implies 503 - 5m \\equiv 0 \\  (\\text{mod }3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"344\" height=\"20\" />, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer.\n</p><p>Rearranging:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd3cbdb141342fd46751b685c16cd059c59c1978.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{lgathered} 5m \\equiv 503 \\equiv 2 \\  (\\text{mod }3) \\\\ m \\equiv 4 \\  (\\text{mod }3) \\qquad \\because 5^{-1} \\equiv 2 \\  (\\text{mod }3)\\\\ m \\equiv 1 \\  (\\text{mod }3) \\\\ \\implies m = 3k + 1 \\end{lgathered}\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"92\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b221cba68f9557fd83aafc35ff8bc601c60390c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$503 - 5m &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/4/f446f4bf4cc868d44dce783df64b3081a72b39ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m &lt;\\frac{503}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"73\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>And because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/4106c78bd0ce6b441e7e44bc727fefd2f41f66d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\leq \\left\\lfloor  \\frac{503}{5}  \\right\\rfloor \\implies m \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"211\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/b/22b2fd30f23e49296157213c33ebc2fd5b341f10.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{lgathered} 3k + 1 \\leq 100 \\\\ 0 \\leq k \\leq 33 \\end{lgathered}\\]\" width=\"100\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> ranges from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342429c4abcdd796779c8255f9e1ae22084bfb9e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\cdot 0+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"15\" />  to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e4c6bf1fc95589e7d96b1affa3428050d5c5f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\cdot 33+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"74\" height=\"15\" />, giving total <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb71b888f27a0fcb48ce814ac0c520bf3c76b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ 034 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> values.\n</p><p>Alternatively, total integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/3/d037f1aa313d30fe7ade693f1b672ed2a68880fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2eb71b888f27a0fcb48ce814ac0c520bf3c76b89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{ 034 }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" /> values.\n</p><p>~vaporwave\n</p><p>Elaborated and reworded by Moisentinel\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because the x-intercept of the equation is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/a/51a96d225c1eae994579a3fb95d40ce2d15932eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2012}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />, and the y-intercept is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61bad80c5e494930687fff88d2ff7acdba2b8e45.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2012}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />, the slope is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/5719969f1536abf3b2d70a2914f7423f2154ab66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\frac{-2012}{12}}{\\frac{2012}{20}} = \\frac{-5}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"94\" height=\"47\" />. Now, notice the first obvious solution: (100,1). From it, we derive all the other solutions by applying the slope in reverse, i.e: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/3/3238819641042b7f7fe47814af98e1c5433cba94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100,1), (97,6), (94,11)...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"196\" height=\"18\" /> Because the solutions are only positive, we can generate only 33 more solutions, so in total we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08598b682a69d60abf3cff1418005512c97ad68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33+1=\\boxed{34}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> solutions.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Quick)\">Solution 4 (Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that a positive integer is divisible by 20 if it ends in 0.\n</p><p>Notice that if a multiple of 12 end in 2, 12 must be multiplied by an integer that ends in 1 or 6.\n</p><p>So let's start checking because 2012 ends in 2, same as 12. \n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f27121969107bf8de193858a1f9192ae58bf734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/2/2f2a6991d2108f237ee451bf37db91cacaf4134e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=6$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d3907b97d00696540606d9cca43802352a726b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=97$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\nWhat is happening? Why doesn't, say, as values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/e/98ee2a665b8e6d4ffa10eddf894dd94f8dc7fa57.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 11, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> work, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/518bb759c50451ed15057d7be542eede3dfb87cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6, 16, 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> work for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> to be an integer (as seen in 2022 CEMC Cayley #21 (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.cemc.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests/2022/2022CayleyContest.pdf\">https://www.cemc.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests/2022/2022CayleyContest.pdf</a>, \n<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.cemc.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests/2022/2022CayleySolution.pdf\">https://www.cemc.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests/2022/2022CayleySolution.pdf</a>)?)\n</p><p>Notice that we can break <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/7/de7d722ae44aabd6082dae349c918b362446ef12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 6, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> down into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/b/0eb7f1010b0f57452128f81e5b005e5ac73f1da1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 5, 10, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"17\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/9/f893e922239141bc95ecdabc7b6205dff6f0df54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20m=2000-12k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"147\" height=\"16\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a member of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f937e43cc288b27afa99b169e651b375d9b1137c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${0, 5, 10, 15...}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>For a number to be divisible by 20, it must be divisible 10, and the quotient (that number divided by 10) must be divisible by 2. This means that the number must end in 0, and its tens digit must be even.\n</p><p>So notice that the tens digit cycle in: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/b/9abb50c5857ac2584bce548e2c81caf9275aa865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0, 4, 8, 2, 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"80\" height=\"17\" />. Each of this is even (notice that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/a/e9a92482c0090dedff5f6074b6030c6946e2a70a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=25$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6d1c308e506388aff9294ceb117f5fd66731525.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2000-12k=1700$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"149\" height=\"16\" />, it cycles again).\n</p><p>So we know that all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, which end in 1 or 6, that make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/9/209e4da7c6d0d5cfd28b8b038083341aa33a330b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2012-12n\\geq20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"16\" /> works.\n</p><p>So values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that belong to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/d/a2dd47c697838442bb284a29da66c408c7a63326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${1, 6, ..., 166}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"17\" /> work. Clearly, that is 34 integer values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2480ac2a3c8d1ad893abd84b2c9a25e3fe923a50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{034}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>~hastapasta\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II\" title=\"2012 AIME II\">2012 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Problem</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"20